(Museum acquires antique clock collection) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] A private collector has donated more than sixty antique clocks to a museum) Tj
T*
(in Dorin. The oldest item is a wooden wall clock with a hand-painted face, and) Tj
T*
(the newest dates from the early part of the last century.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Staff will spend the winter cleaning and cataloguing the collection.) Tj
T*
(Several clocks still work, but most will be displayed with their mechanisms) Tj
T*
(stopped to reduce wear.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] The museum plans to open a small exhibition in the spring. A clockmaker has) Tj
T*
(offered to give a public talk about repair techniques, and the museum is looking) Tj
T*
(for volunteers to help record the collection.) Tj
